  "findings": [
    "Live application heap at the traversal peak is 495.0-510.3 MB across three rounds at 750,438 live views: 637-657 bytes per view. The heavy peak is real live data, not allocator retention.",
    "After release the live heap returns to 17.8-18.1 MB while RSS stays at 489.5-559.8 MB: 96.4-96.8 percent of retained RSS is allocator-held free arena.",
    "Peak RSS rises +38.1 and +32.0 MB between rounds while the live peak stays flat, so the inter-round slope on the heavy fixture is allocator retention and is 3-4x larger than the 10 MB/pass recorded on the light readdir-only fixture.",
    "Released PSS minus indexed_baseline PSS is 476.4 / 514.8 / 546.7 MiB against the 256 MiB budget: missed by 1.86x, 2.01x, 2.14x, and the miss grows each round.",
    "Both remedies are therefore required and are complementary: bounding live view count cannot lower released RSS, and allocator tuning cannot lower a 507 MB live peak."
